5
00:00:17.854 --> 00:00:21.514
which is much more than a show to me.

6
00:00:21.514 --> 00:00:25.340
There's historical references of pop culture

7
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:29.800
in a time that we remember so well,

8
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.963
the Pam and Tommy days.

9
00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:37.830
But this show has such an interesting debate behind it.

10
00:00:37.885 --> 00:00:39.469
Tell me about the show.

11
00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:41.270
Why is it important to you?

12
00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.012
What is the takeaway here?

13
00:00:43.012 --> 00:00:46.000
Well, for me, there was this kind of whisper

14
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.930 line:15%
of an idea that Pam Anderson somehow was a participant

15
00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:53.730 line:15%
or was involved in some way

16
00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.670
in this tape being out in the world.

17
00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.500
And I was struck, in reading all of the scripts,

18
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.830 line:15%
that she actually is the survivor of a crime

19
00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.930 line:15%
and we haven't treated...

20
00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.290 line:15%
