25
00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:21.163
Nope.

26
00:01:21.163 --> 00:01:22.620
A judge almost made the decision

27
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.980 line:15%
that her body kind of belonged to the collective,

28
00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.670 line:15%
and not to herself,

29
00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:31.000 line:15%
which is something that's kind of hard for us to...

30
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.310
It's hard for me to wrap...

31
00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.143
Right?

32
00:01:33.143 --> 00:01:33.976
It's really hard to wrap your head around.

33
00:01:33.976 --> 00:01:35.730
It's hard for me to wrap my head around that.

34
00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:40.680
I think there is such rich conversation in this show

35
00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:45.224
about where is consent in all of this?

36
00:01:45.224 --> 00:01:46.600
Yeah.

37
00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.300
Well, and I love that you're bringing that up

38
00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.340
because consent, you know, for me personally,

39
00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.220
I think consent is the sun.

40
00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.330
Like, everything revolves sort of around consent.

41
00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:02.286
And as soon as it's a choice that someone's making,

42
00:02:02.286 --> 00:02:03.810
God bless.

43
00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.150
When it's not a choice and I'm not in control

44
00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:10.687
